lace-hall.ldr","status":"local_definition_not_root_reachable","design_review":{"scope":"B-owned Round Table Hall only. Latest main root and external royal stairs, paired thrones and dais are preserved and not copied.","local_floor":"24 x 24 stud base; visible floor top Y=0 LDU and stud plane Y=-8 LDU.","open_structure":"Front and both sides are open colonnades around a retained rear support wall. Two 3659 arch bays are retained on the front and on each side (front centers X=60,380; side centers Z=60,380). Remaining bays stay open between full-height 2x2 stone piers. At each arch foot, the upper pier block is replaced by the arch; dark-stone capitals remain on the unobstructed pier tops.","roof_support":"The existing two removable roof modules, their slopes, ridge grips, and chandelier are retained. Timber transverse front ties, side eave seats, rear support wall, and surviving full-height piers connect to the roofs. Seven 1x1 masonry pier blocks under the eave seats bridge the two arch-replaced bays without intersecting the arch bodies.","table_and_seats":"The four-brick round table, twelve knight seats, and distinct raised perilous seat are retained unchanged.","removal_review":"Closed local pose. Each roof module lifts vertically; the left module carries the chandelier. Nominal named-stud checks report each lifted roof as one component and the remaining hall as one component with either or both modules removed. Vertical extraction path, hand access, clutch force, and physical roof seating are not mechanically tested.","validation":"Current geometry: one connected component with both roofs installed; one component in the hall with either or both roofs removed; each lifted module including the chandelier is one component; zero nominal body overlaps and zero native DAT surface-crossing candidates. This is a digital nominal check, not physical assembly, clutch, load, or complete solid-interference verification."},"instances":[{"id":"B-00001","group":"B-floor-base","pa